  "title": "Erdős Problem #25",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $n_1<n_2<\\cdots$ be an arbitrary sequence of integers, each with an associated residue class $a_i\\pmod{n_i}$. Let $A$ be the set of integers $n$ such that for every $i$ either $n<n_i$ or $n\not\\equiv a_i\\pmod{n_i}$. Must the logarithmic density of $A$ exist?",
